      "writtenOn": "2017-04-27T07:55:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t understand how this works.\n\nThis number is saying we received 7892 packets on wlan0. But adding together the 7th field of the lines above with v4-wlan0, we see that v4-wlan0 received 5+25+6717+1041+2870 \u003d 10658 packets. If we subtract 7892 we end up with -2766 packets, which seems wrong.\n\nSimilarly, with bytes, the stats say we received 11058671 bytes on wlan0. But if we add together all the bytes on v4-wlan0, we get 256+30312+9398432+1448660+9702 \u003d 10887362 bytes.\n\nBut the unit test says that wlan0 should count 15229 bytes, and I can\u0027t figure out how to get there. If we take 10887362 (bytes on v4-wlan0) and add 20*10658 (packets on v4-wlan0), we end up with a delta of (10887362+(20×10658))−11058671 \u003d 41851.\n\nWhat am I doing wrong?",
